.IX Title "LTPADMIN 1"
.TH LTPADMIN 1 2025-11-26 "perl v5.38.2" "LTP executables"
.\" For nroff, turn off justification.  Always turn off hyphenation; it makes
.\" way too many mistakes in technical documents.
.if n .ad l
.nh
.SH NAME
ltpadmin \- ION Licklider Transmission Protocol (LTP) administration interface
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IX Header "SYNOPSIS"
\&\fBltpadmin\fR [ \fIcommands_filename\fR | . | ! ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
\&\fBltpadmin\fR configures, starts, manages, and stops LTP operations for
the local ION node.
.PP
It operates in response to LTP configuration commands found in the file
\&\fIcommands_filename\fR, if provided; if not, \fBltpadmin\fR prints
a simple prompt (:) so that the user may type commands
directly into standard input.  If \fIcommands_filename\fR is a period (.), the
effect is the same as if a command file containing the single command 'x'
were passed to \fBltpadmin\fR \-\- that is, the ION node's \fIltpclock\fR task, 
\&\fIltpmeter\fR tasks, and link service adapter tasks are stopped.
If \fIcommands_filename\fR is an exclamation point (!), that effect is
reversed: the ION node's \fIltpclock\fR task, \fIltpmeter\fR tasks, and link
service adapter tasks are restarted.
.PP
The format of commands for \fIcommands_filename\fR can be queried from \fBltpadmin\fR
with the 'h' or '?' commands at the prompt.  The commands are documented in
\&\fBltprc\fR\|(5).
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.IX Header "EXIT STATUS"
.IP """0"" Successful completion of LTP administration." 4
.IX Item """0"" Successful completion of LTP administration."
.SH EXAMPLES
.IX Header "EXAMPLES"
.PD 0
.IP ltpadmin 4
.IX Item "ltpadmin"
.PD
Enter interactive LTP configuration command entry mode.
.IP "ltpadmin host1.ltp" 4
.IX Item "ltpadmin host1.ltp"
Execute all configuration commands in \fIhost1.ltp\fR, then terminate immediately.
.IP "ltpadmin ." 4
.IX Item "ltpadmin ."
Stop all LTP operations on the local node.
.SH FILES
.IX Header "FILES"
See \fBltprc\fR\|(5) for details of the LTP configuration commands.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.IX Header "ENVIRONMENT"
No environment variables apply.
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
.IX Header "DIAGNOSTICS"
\&\fBNote\fR: all ION administration utilities expect source file input to be
lines of ASCII text that are NL-delimited.  If you edit the ltprc file on
a Windows machine, be sure to \fBuse dos2unix to convert it to Unix text format\fR
before presenting it to \fBltpadmin\fR.  Otherwise \fBltpadmin\fR will detect syntax
errors and will not function satisfactorily.
.PP
The following diagnostics may be issued to the logfile ion.log:
.IP "ltpadmin can't attach to ION." 4
.IX Item "ltpadmin can't attach to ION."
There is no SDR data store for \fIltpadmin\fR to use.  You should run \fBionadmin\fR\|(1)
first, to set up an SDR data store for ION.
.IP "Can't open command file..." 4
.IX Item "Can't open command file..."
The \fIcommands_filename\fR specified in the command line doesn't exist.
.PP
Various errors that don't cause \fBltpadmin\fR to fail but are noted in the
\&\fBion.log\fR log file may be caused by improperly formatted commands
given at the prompt or in the \fIcommands_filename\fR file.
Please see \fBltprc\fR\|(5) for details.
.SH BUGS
.IX Header "BUGS"
Report bugs to <https://github.com/nasa\-jpl/ION\-DTN/issues>
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.IX Header "SEE ALSO"
\&\fBltpmeter\fR\|(1), \fBltprc\fR\|(5)
